%N A087517 Consider pairs (i,j) such that j*prime(i)# - prime(i+2) and j*prime(i)# - prime(i+1) are consecutive primes and 0 < j < prime(i+1), where prime(r)# = r-th primorial number (A002110). Sequence gives j values.
%e A087517 2*(2*3) - 7 =  5, 2*(2*3) - 5 =  7, with 5 and 7 consecutive primes, so (i,j) = (2,2) and a(1) = 2;
%e A087517 3*(2*3) - 7 = 11, 3*(2*3) - 5 = 13, with 11 and 13 consecutive primes, so (i,j) = (2,3) and a(2)=3;
%e A087517 4*(2*3) - 7 = 17, 4*(2*3) - 5 = 19, with 17 and 19 consecutive primes, so (i,j) = (2,4) and a(3)=3;
%e A087517 1*(2*3*5) - 11 =  19, 1*(2*3*5) - 7 =  23, 19 and 23 consecutive primes, so (i,j) = (3,1) and a(4)=1;
%e A087517 3*(2*3*5) - 11 =  79, 3*(2*3*5) - 7 =  83, 79 and 83 consecutive primes, so (i,j) = (3,3) and a(5)=3;
%e A087517 4*(2*3*5) - 11 = 109, 4*(2*3*5) - 7 = 113, 109 and 113 consecutive primes, so (i,j) = (3,4) and a(5)=4;
%e A087517 ...
%Y A087517 Cf. A087516 (prime(i) values).
%K A087517 nonn,changed
